WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:09.307
The 192-fiber trunks end in the network rows,
at the DCN patch panel racks.

2
00:00:10.057 --> 00:00:13.854
This video follows them there, and on to the
spines.

3
00:00:15.204 --> 00:00:22.065
We will look at the patch panel rack, how to
find the right panel and lane, how to land a

4
00:00:22.065 --> 00:00:28.772
trunk, what the shuffle module does, the cords
to the spines, and one complete example.

5
00:00:32.922 --> 00:00:41.946
A DCN patch panel rack, or DCN-PP, is a
passive rack in network rows one and two.

6
00:00:42.696 --> 00:00:46.600
Passive means it has no switches, only panels.

7
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:55.356
It holds eight patch panels, each four rack
units tall, laid out like the end of row

8
00:00:55.356 --> 00:01:00.523
panel: twelve rows, and columns A to L with
two ports each.

9
00:01:01.873 --> 00:01:07.931
Large sites like this one use two-by-two
shuffle modules in these panels.

10
00:01:08.681 --> 00:01:11.135
We will see what they do in a moment.

11
00:01:12.485 --> 00:01:16.602
The 192-fiber trunks land on the back.

12
00:01:17.352 --> 00:01:21.043
Short MPO cords leave the front for the
spines.

13
00:01:25.193 --> 00:01:32.702
For every 192-fiber trunk, the trunk landing
sheet answers three questions.

14
00:01:33.702 --> 00:01:34.875
Which rack?

15
00:01:35.625 --> 00:01:37.865
You learned this in lesson eight.

16
00:01:38.615 --> 00:01:45.463
The column picks the patch panel pair, and the
end of row rack's spot picks north or south.

17
00:01:46.813 --> 00:01:48.072
Which panel?

18
00:01:48.822 --> 00:01:55.883
End of row racks in rows three to fourteen
land in the panel at RU thirty-five.

19
00:01:56.633 --> 00:02:02.159
Rows fifteen to twenty-six land in the panel
at RU thirty-nine.

20
00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:04.725
Which lane?

21
00:02:05.475 --> 00:02:11.405
The sheet writes it like this: AIO-PP3, CD,
number one.

22
00:02:12.155 --> 00:02:18.960
That means the trunk's slot number on the
panel, the pair of columns it uses, and lane

23
00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.859
one or two of that pair.

24
00:02:22.209 --> 00:02:31.160
For example, end of row rack 511 lands in the
RU thirty-five panel, slot three, columns C

25
00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.769
and D, lane one.

26
00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:38.021
The same panel and lane apply to all eight of
its columns.

27
00:02:42.171 --> 00:02:44.923
This is the back of one patch panel.

28
00:02:45.673 --> 00:02:49.598
Again, facing the rear, column A is on the
right.

29
00:02:50.348 --> 00:02:52.033
Work right to left.

30
00:02:53.433 --> 00:02:56.335
A trunk uses one pair of columns.

31
00:02:57.085 --> 00:03:02.119
Its odd legs go in the first column of the
pair, here column A.

32
00:03:02.869 --> 00:03:06.859
Its even legs go in the second column, column
B.

33
00:03:08.209 --> 00:03:15.796
The legs go up: legs one and two in row one,
up to legs twenty-three and twenty-four in row

34
00:03:15.796 --> 00:03:16.379
twelve.

35
00:03:17.729 --> 00:03:21.868
Each trunk uses only one lane of the column
pair.

36
00:03:22.618 --> 00:03:27.674
The next end of row rack's trunk uses the lane
right beside it.

37
00:03:29.024 --> 00:03:34.229
Legs nineteen to twenty-four, in the top three
rows, are spares.

38
00:03:34.979 --> 00:03:38.521
And one panel holds twelve end of row trunks.

39
00:03:42.671 --> 00:03:47.513
Behind each column pair sits a two-by-two
shuffle module.

40
00:03:48.263 --> 00:03:54.819
It takes two eight-fiber inputs on the back,
and gives two eight-fiber outputs on the

41
00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:55.282
front.

42
00:03:56.632 --> 00:04:01.432
The trick is that each output carries fibers
from both inputs.

43
00:04:02.182 --> 00:04:04.870
The two inputs are shuffled together.

44
00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:10.039
There are two of these shuffles inside every
module.

45
00:04:11.389 --> 00:04:18.344
That is why the two lanes of a column pair
must hold trunks from two different end of row

46
00:04:18.344 --> 00:04:18.813
racks.

47
00:04:19.563 --> 00:04:24.299
The shuffle spreads every TPU rack across all
the spines.

48
00:04:25.649 --> 00:04:27.398
One important check.

49
00:04:28.148 --> 00:04:34.505
Large sites use part number 760262482.

50
00:04:35.255 --> 00:04:41.613
If a module reads 760262479, stop.

51
00:04:42.363 --> 00:04:47.632
That is a four-by-four module, and these
instructions do not apply.

52
00:04:51.782 --> 00:04:54.129
Now the front of the same panel.

53
00:04:54.879 --> 00:04:57.631
Each module has four front ports.

54
00:04:58.981 --> 00:05:06.680
In every module, those four ports go to spines
one, two, three and four of that patch panel's

55
00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.005
group, in order.

56
00:05:09.355 --> 00:05:15.136
Each port takes one eight-fiber MPO cord to
one spine port.

57
00:05:16.486 --> 00:05:19.771
Patch panel A feeds spines one to four.

58
00:05:20.521 --> 00:05:22.591
B feeds five to eight.

59
00:05:23.341 --> 00:05:28.930
And so on, up to H, which feeds spines
twenty-nine to thirty-two.

60
00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:36.893
Each row of the panel lands on the next line
card port of those same four spines.

61
00:05:37.643 --> 00:05:41.953
A line card is a slot in the spine that holds
ports.

62
00:05:42.703 --> 00:05:46.649
The cutsheet gives the exact port for every
cord.

63
00:05:50.799 --> 00:05:57.818
Let us put it all together for one trunk: end
of row rack 1411, column E.

64
00:05:59.018 --> 00:06:00.191
Which rack?

65
00:06:00.941 --> 00:06:03.501
Column E means patch panel E.

66
00:06:04.251 --> 00:06:06.854
Spot eleven means the north rack.

67
00:06:07.604 --> 00:06:09.780
That is rack 207.

68
00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.389
Which panel?

69
00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:19.389
Row fourteen is in rows three to fourteen, so
the RU thirty-five panel.

70
00:06:20.739 --> 00:06:21.955
Which lane?

71
00:06:22.705 --> 00:06:27.783
The landing sheet says slot twelve, columns K
and L, lane two.

72
00:06:29.133 --> 00:06:37.985
The K and L module mixes this trunk with slot
eleven in lane one, which is end of row rack

73
00:06:37.985 --> 00:06:38.477
1311.

74
00:06:39.227 --> 00:06:41.509
Two different end of row racks.

75
00:06:42.259 --> 00:06:43.305
Correct.

76
00:06:44.655 --> 00:06:51.947
And on the front, that module's four ports go
to spines seventeen, eighteen, nineteen and

77
00:06:51.947 --> 00:06:55.961
twenty, at the line card port the cutsheet
gives.

78
00:07:00.111 --> 00:07:07.080
In lesson nine of the course, practice using
the landing sheet to find the rack, panel and

79
00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.093
lane for different trunks.

